< \emph{Utility ratio} $q=U(\hat b)/\max_b U(b)$ with expected profit $U(b)=p(b)(v-b)$ under held-out probabilities $p$. The calculator returns $\arg\max_b \hat p(b)(v-b)$ and scores $q=0.981$; random choice scores 0.711. \emph{Gap recovered} at budget $c$ is $(q(c)-q(0))/(q_{\text{calc}}-q(0))$; the \emph{dollar gap} uses $U$. Intervals resample the 18 value families within each product (2{,}000 draws).
